2 {\cf20 // About imgui_impl_opengl3_loader.h:}\par
3 {\cf20 //}\par
4 {\cf20 // We embed our own OpenGL loader to not require user to provide their own or to have to use ours,}\par
5 {\cf20 // which proved to be endless problems for users.}\par
6 {\cf20 // Our loader is custom-generated, based on gl3w but automatically filtered to only include}\par
7 {\cf20 // enums/functions that we use in our imgui_impl_opengl3.cpp source file in order to be small.}\par
8 {\cf20 //}\par
9 {\cf20 // YOU SHOULD NOT NEED TO INCLUDE/USE THIS DIRECTLY. THIS IS USED BY imgui_impl_opengl3.cpp ONLY.}\par
10 {\cf20 // THE REST OF YOUR APP SHOULD USE A DIFFERENT GL LOADER: ANY GL LOADER OF YOUR CHOICE.}\par
11 {\cf20 //}\par
12 {\cf20 // IF YOU GET BUILD ERRORS IN THIS FILE (commonly macro redefinitions or function redefinitions):}\par
13 {\cf20 // IT LIKELY MEANS THAT YOU ARE BUILDING 'imgui_impl_opengl3.cpp' OR INCLUDING 'imgui_impl_opengl3_loader.h'}\par
14 {\cf20 // IN THE SAME COMPILATION UNIT AS ONE OF YOUR FILE WHICH IS USING A THIRD-PARTY OPENGL LOADER.}\par
15 {\cf20 // (e.g. COULD HAPPEN IF YOU ARE DOING A UNITY/JUMBO BUILD, OR INCLUDING .CPP FILES FROM OTHERS)}\par
16 {\cf20 // YOU SHOULD NOT BUILD BOTH IN THE SAME COMPILATION UNIT.}\par
17 {\cf20 // BUT IF YOU REALLY WANT TO, you can '#define IMGUI_IMPL_OPENGL_LOADER_CUSTOM' and imgui_impl_opengl3.cpp}\par
18 {\cf20 // WILL NOT BE USING OUR LOADER, AND INSTEAD EXPECT ANOTHER/YOUR LOADER TO BE AVAILABLE IN THE COMPILATION UNIT.}\par
19 {\cf20 //}\par
20 {\cf20 // Regenerate with:}\par
21 {\cf20 //   python3 gl3w_gen.py --output ../imgui/backends/imgui_impl_opengl3_loader.h --ref ../imgui/backends/imgui_impl_opengl3.cpp ./extra_symbols.txt}\par
